Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:09:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): accept a typed model ID when a provider uses a
 custom Base URL

The BYOK docs say to set a custom Base URL for self-hosted or proxied
models, but OpenAI, Anthropic and the other catalog adapters only offer
their curated model IDs. A server such as Ollama or vLLM rejects those
names, so Test Connection (GET /models) passes and every detector run
then fails with a 404.

A Base URL on another host than the adapter's default now gets the
free-text model input the pass-through adapters already use, with the
catalog IDs kept as suggestions. The adapter's own host, with any path,
keeps the dropdown.

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
